(window.XZ_MANUAL_CHAPTERS=window.XZ_MANUAL_CHAPTERS||{})["hardware"]="<header class=\"mc-head\"><p class=\"mc-eyebrow\">Start here<\/p><h2 class=\"mc-title\" tabindex=\"-1\">Controls on the player<\/h2><p class=\"mc-lede\">Which buttons, pads and knobs do something new, and what each one does with XZ Mods running.<\/p><p class=\"applies\" data-applies=\"both\">Applies to <b>MODERN and CLASSIC<\/b><\/p><\/header><p>XZ Mods leaves every control on the XDJ-XZ doing its stock job unless this page says otherwise. This page covers only the controls whose behaviour XZ Mods changes or adds, and the ones you use to drive MODS. For everything else, the XDJ-XZ operating instructions still apply.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-the-top-panel\" data-anchor=\"the-top-panel\">The top panel<\/h3>\n<p>The picture shows the XDJ-XZ from straight above, rendered from a true-scale model of the player.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf mf--hw\" id=\"f-hardware-1\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">XDJ-XZ top panel<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/f62b41bb6c224c25.webp\" width=\"1600\" height=\"863\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"The XDJ-XZ from above: the browse section with the touch screen at the top centre, a deck on each side and the four-channel mixer under the screen.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"50.000\" data-y=\"18.772\" aria-label=\"1: Touch screen\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-1-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"58.750\" data-y=\"6.605\" aria-label=\"2: MENU (UTILITY)\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-1-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"60.000\" data-y=\"10.660\" aria-label=\"3: BACK\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-1-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"64.875\" data-y=\"14.832\" aria-label=\"4: Rotary selector\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-1-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"64.875\" data-y=\"20.626\" aria-label=\"5: SHORTCUT\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-1-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"35.250\" data-y=\"9.502\" aria-label=\"6: Button above LINK\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-1-6\">6<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"7\" data-x=\"35.250\" data-y=\"12.746\" aria-label=\"7: LINK\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-1-7\">7<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"8\" data-x=\"35.375\" data-y=\"25.029\" aria-label=\"8: TIME MODE and DECK QUANTIZE\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-1-8\">8<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"9\" data-x=\"65.062\" data-y=\"27.578\" aria-label=\"9: LOAD 1, LOAD 2\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-1-9\">9<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"10\" data-x=\"17.562\" data-y=\"54.461\" aria-label=\"10: Left deck\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-1-10\">10<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"11\" data-x=\"82.438\" data-y=\"54.461\" aria-label=\"11: Right deck\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-1-11\">11<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"12\" data-x=\"50.000\" data-y=\"66.860\" aria-label=\"12: Mixer channels 3 1 2 4\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-1-12\">12<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>The XDJ-XZ from above: the browse section with the touch screen at the top centre, a deck on each side and the four-channel mixer under the screen.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-hardware-1-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>Touch screen<\/b> <span>Shows the play screen in the interface you chose (MODERN or CLASSIC) and the MODS menu. Every MODS control also answers touch.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-hardware-1-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>MENU (UTILITY)<\/b> <span>Press: opens MODS where the screen has no MENU job of its own. Hold: opens the player's own UTILITY, as on a stock XDJ-XZ.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-hardware-1-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>BACK<\/b> <span>Goes up one level, in MODS too.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-hardware-1-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>Rotary selector<\/b> <span>Turn to move the highlight in MODS, push to select. It drives every MODS page, so you never need the touch screen.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-hardware-1-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>SHORTCUT<\/b> <span>Opens the SHORTCUT screen as on a stock player. A short MENU on that screen opens MODS.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-hardware-1-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>Button above LINK<\/b> <span>The media button directly above LINK. XZ Mods lets you choose what it does, alone and with SHIFT.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"7\" id=\"f-hardware-1-7\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">7<\/span><div><b>LINK<\/b> <span>Its stock job. It can also switch the VJ.Tools view on and off.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"8\" id=\"f-hardware-1-8\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">8<\/span><div><b>TIME MODE and DECK QUANTIZE<\/b> <span>Stock on decks 1 and 2. While a side drives deck 3 or 4 they also reach the software decks.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"9\" id=\"f-hardware-1-9\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">9<\/span><div><b>LOAD 1, LOAD 2<\/b> <span>Load into the deck that side controls now: deck 1 or 3 on the left, deck 2 or 4 on the right.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"10\" id=\"f-hardware-1-10\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">10<\/span><div><b>Left deck<\/b> <span>Controls deck 1, or deck 3 after you press SHIFT twice.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"11\" id=\"f-hardware-1-11\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">11<\/span><div><b>Right deck<\/b> <span>Controls deck 2, or deck 4 after you press SHIFT twice.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"12\" id=\"f-hardware-1-12\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">12<\/span><div><b>Mixer channels 3 1 2 4<\/b> <span>Decks 3 and 4 play through CH3 and CH4 over the loopback cable.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<h3 id=\"m-browse-section-keys\" data-anchor=\"browse-section-keys\">Browse section keys<\/h3>\n<div class=\"mn\" data-iface=\"modern\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Browse section keys\"><ol class=\"mn-scenes\"><li data-flow=\"b-browse-keys\" data-video=\"assets/manual/nav/b-browse-keys.mp4\" data-poster=\"assets/manual/nav/b-browse-keys.webp\" data-w=\"1280\" data-h=\"480\" data-seconds=\"8.512\" data-title=\"Browse section keys\"><ol class=\"mn-steps\"><li data-t=\"500\">Open SOURCE (<span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"back\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/back.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"76.49\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BACK<\/span><\/span> at the top of a list)<\/li><li data-t=\"1000\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span><\/li><li data-t=\"1500\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span><\/li><li data-t=\"2000\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"info\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/info.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"54.02\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">INFO<\/span><\/span><\/li><li data-t=\"2500\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span><\/li><li data-t=\"3000\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"back\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/back.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"76.49\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BACK<\/span><\/span><\/li><li data-t=\"3500\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span><\/li><li data-t=\"4000\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shortcut\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shortcut.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"114.93\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHORTCUT<\/span><\/span><\/li><li data-t=\"4500\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span><\/li><li data-t=\"5000\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span><\/li><li data-t=\"5500\">Hold <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span> for a second<\/li><li data-t=\"7000\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"back\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/back.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"76.49\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BACK<\/span><\/span><\/li><\/ol><\/li><\/ol><\/div>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Key<\/th><th>Action with XZ Mods<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span> press<\/td><td>Opens MODS on the play screen, the SOURCE screen, the INFO screen and the SHORTCUT screen <span class=\"tag tag--experimental\">experimental<\/span>. Everywhere else it keeps its stock job. In MODS it closes MODS.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span> hold<\/td><td>Opens the player's own UTILITY, in both interfaces.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"back\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/back.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"76.49\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BACK<\/span><\/span><\/td><td>Goes up one level. In MODS it steps from an open item to its page, then to the section rail.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"rotary-turn\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/rotary-turn.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"33\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">TURN<\/span><\/span> Rotary selector, turn<\/td><td>Moves the highlight to the next card, row or button in MODS. On a beat jump pair, after a push, it steps the jump size.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"rotary-push\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/rotary-push.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"33\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">PUSH<\/span><\/span> Rotary selector, push<\/td><td>Opens or changes the highlighted item in MODS.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"above-link\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/above-link.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"54.4\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BUTTON ABOVE LINK<\/span><\/span><\/td><td>Does what you chose in MODS &gt; PLAY &gt; BUTTON ABOVE LINK. The default is INTERFACE.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> + <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"above-link\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/above-link.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"54.4\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BUTTON ABOVE LINK<\/span><\/span><\/td><td>Hold <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> on either deck and press it. Does the second choice on the same page. The default is ITS OWN JOB.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"link\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/link.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"54.02\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">LINK<\/span><\/span><\/td><td>Its stock job. With the screen switch key set to LINK it also switches the VJ.Tools view on and off.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shortcut\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shortcut.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"114.93\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHORTCUT<\/span><\/span><\/td><td>Opens the SHORTCUT screen. In MODERN this is MODERN's own SHORTCUT screen.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"load\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/load.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"100.66\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">LOAD<\/span><\/span><\/td><td>Loads the highlighted track into the deck that side controls: deck 1 or 3, deck 2 or 4.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"time-mode\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/time-mode.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"108.29\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">TIME MODE<\/span><\/span>, <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"deck-quantize\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/deck-quantize.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"144.23\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">DECK QUANTIZE<\/span><\/span><\/td><td>Stock on decks 1 and 2. For decks 3 and 4, see <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"performance\" data-anchor=\"quantize\">Quantize<\/a> and <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"four-decks\">Four decks<\/a>.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>A short press of <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span> keeps the job the player's own firmware gives it wherever there is one. This table comes from the firmware itself:<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Where you are<\/th><th>Short press of <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span><\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>The MODS menu is open<\/td><td>Closes MODS<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>A game is on screen<\/td><td>The game's own key<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The VJ.Tools view is on screen<\/td><td>As before<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>A menu, popup or dialog is open<\/td><td>Works or closes the open menu<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>A track list (browse, playlist, search, history)<\/td><td>The sort menu or the track menu<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>TAG LIST<\/td><td>LIST MENU<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The play screen in GRID ADJUST<\/td><td>The beat grid menu<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The play screen<\/td><td>Opens MODS <span class=\"tag tag--experimental\">experimental<\/span><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The SOURCE screen<\/td><td>Opens MODS <span class=\"tag tag--experimental\">experimental<\/span><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The track INFO screen<\/td><td>Opens MODS <span class=\"tag tag--experimental\">experimental<\/span><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The SHORTCUT screen<\/td><td>Opens MODS <span class=\"tag tag--experimental\">experimental<\/span><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The player's own UTILITY<\/td><td>Closes UTILITY<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Any other screen<\/td><td>The screen's own job<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<h3 id=\"m-the-button-above-link\" data-anchor=\"the-button-above-link\">The button above LINK<\/h3>\n<p>The XDJ-XZ has a media button directly above <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"link\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/link.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"54.02\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">LINK<\/span><\/span>. On a stock player it opens the library of a computer or phone connected to the player. XZ Mods gives it two slots: a plain press, and a press while <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> is held on either deck. Set them in MODS &gt; PLAY &gt; BUTTON ABOVE LINK.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mn\" data-iface=\"modern\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"The button above LINK\"><ol class=\"mn-scenes\"><li data-flow=\"physical-above-link\" data-video=\"assets/manual/nav/physical-above-link.mp4\" data-poster=\"assets/manual/nav/physical-above-link.webp\" data-w=\"1280\" data-h=\"480\" data-seconds=\"2.112\" data-title=\"The button above LINK\"><ol class=\"mn-steps\"><li data-t=\"500\">Press the button above <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"link\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/link.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"54.02\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">LINK<\/span><\/span><\/li><li data-t=\"800\">Press the button above <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"link\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/link.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"54.02\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">LINK<\/span><\/span><\/li><\/ol><\/li><\/ol><\/div>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-hardware-2\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODS · BUTTON ABOVE LINK<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/33182e11dce0e442.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Both slots at their defaults. A press switches the interface, and SHIFT + press keeps the button&#x27;s own job.\" data-iface=\"modern\"><img src=\"manual/shots/00b0f268d5ded1d2.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Both slots at their defaults. A press switches the interface, and SHIFT + press keeps the button&#x27;s own job.\" data-iface=\"classic\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"49.750\" data-y=\"19.167\" aria-label=\"1: Media buttons\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-2-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"23.125\" data-y=\"19.167\" aria-label=\"2: PRESS\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-2-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"52.500\" data-y=\"42.500\" aria-label=\"3: What it does\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-2-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"28.125\" data-y=\"47.500\" aria-label=\"4: SHIFT + PRESS\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-2-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"66.875\" data-y=\"70.833\" aria-label=\"5: What it does\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-2-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"23.750\" data-y=\"88.542\" aria-label=\"6: Dock\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-2-6\">6<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>Both slots at their defaults. A press switches the interface, and SHIFT + press keeps the button's own job.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-hardware-2-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>Media buttons<\/b> <span>The four media buttons in the player's order from the top, left to right: the button above LINK, highlighted, then LINK, USB 1 and USB 2.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-hardware-2-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>PRESS<\/b> <span>What a plain press does. The filled choice is the current one.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-hardware-2-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>What it does<\/b> <span>One line explaining the current PRESS choice.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-hardware-2-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>SHIFT + PRESS<\/b> <span>What the button does while SHIFT is held on either deck.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-hardware-2-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>What it does<\/b> <span>One line explaining the current SHIFT + PRESS choice.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-hardware-2-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>Dock<\/b> <span>Explains the highlighted choice before you pick it.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Choice<\/th><th>What the button does<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>MODS MENU<\/td><td>Opens and closes MODS. MODS then works with the rotary selector and <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"back\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/back.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"76.49\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BACK<\/span><\/span>.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>ITS OWN JOB<\/td><td>The stock job: the screen for playing a computer's or phone's library. In MODERN the player's own screen for it takes over until you are back on the play screen.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>INTERFACE<\/td><td>Switches between MODERN and CLASSIC, with the same notice as MODS &gt; SCREEN.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>VJ.TOOLS SCREEN<\/td><td>Switches the VJ.Tools screen on and off. Without an enabled, connected VJ.Tools link it says so instead.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>STEMS<\/td><td>Does what the STEMS button on the screen does: steps the stem buttons through their places in 2 DECKS, and shows or hides them in MODERN's 4 DECKS.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>DECK VIEW<\/td><td>Steps DECK VIEW: 2 DECKS, 4 DECKS in number order 1 2 3 4, 4 DECKS in mixer order 3 1 2 4, then 2 DECKS again. It saves the choice and shows the new view in a short notice.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>NOTHING<\/td><td>The button does nothing.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<aside class=\"callout callout--tip\"><b>Tip<\/b><p>With the default INTERFACE on a plain press, you can always get back to MODS without touching the screen: press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span> on the play screen, or switch interface with the button above <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"link\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/link.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"54.02\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">LINK<\/span><\/span> and press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span> there.<\/p><\/aside>\n<h3 id=\"m-link-and-the-vj-tools-view\" data-anchor=\"link-and-the-vj-tools-view\">LINK and the VJ.Tools view<\/h3>\n<p>When VJ.Tools on a computer is connected, the player's screen can show the VJ.Tools view instead of the play screen. MODS &gt; CONNECT &gt; VJ.TOOLS has a SCREEN SWITCH KEY with two choices:<\/p>\n<div class=\"mn\" data-iface=\"modern\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"LINK and the VJ.Tools view\"><ol class=\"mn-scenes\"><li data-flow=\"vj-tools\" data-video=\"assets/manual/nav/vj-tools.mp4\" data-poster=\"assets/manual/nav/vj-tools.webp\" data-w=\"1280\" data-h=\"480\" data-seconds=\"3.452\" data-title=\"LINK and the VJ.Tools view\"><ol class=\"mn-steps\"><li data-t=\"500\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span><\/li><li data-t=\"1000\">Tap <strong>CONNECT<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"1520\">Tap <strong>VJ.TOOLS<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"2040\">Turn <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"rotary\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/rotary.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"33\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">ROTARY SELECTOR<\/span><\/span> 2 clicks clockwise<\/li><\/ol><\/li><\/ol><\/div>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Choice<\/th><th>What switches the VJ.Tools view<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>LINK (default)<\/td><td>Pressing <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"link\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/link.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"54.02\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">LINK<\/span><\/span>. <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"link\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/link.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"54.02\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">LINK<\/span><\/span> also keeps its stock job.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>ONSCREEN<\/td><td>A VJ.Tools button on the screen, in the corner opposite MODS.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>To switch the view with the button above <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"link\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/link.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"54.02\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">LINK<\/span><\/span> instead, set that button to VJ.TOOLS SCREEN. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"connect\">Connect and DJ profiles<\/a> for the connection itself.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-deck-keys\" data-anchor=\"deck-keys\">Deck keys<\/h3>\n<p>The picture shows the left deck from above. The right deck has the same controls in the same places.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mn\" data-iface=\"modern\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Deck keys\"><ol class=\"mn-scenes\"><li data-flow=\"b-master-tempo\" data-video=\"assets/manual/nav/b-master-tempo.mp4\" data-poster=\"assets/manual/nav/b-master-tempo.webp\" data-w=\"1280\" data-h=\"480\" data-seconds=\"2.352\" data-title=\"KEY SYNC, then MASTER TEMPO\"><ol class=\"mn-steps\"><li data-t=\"500\">Hold <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> on the left deck and press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"sync\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/sync.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"75.39\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SYNC<\/span><\/span> on the left deck<\/li><li data-t=\"1040\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"master-tempo\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/master-tempo.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"142.24\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MASTER TEMPO<\/span><\/span> on the left deck<\/li><\/ol><\/li><li data-flow=\"physical-key-sync\" data-video=\"assets/manual/nav/physical-key-sync.mp4\" data-poster=\"assets/manual/nav/physical-key-sync.webp\" data-w=\"1280\" data-h=\"480\" data-seconds=\"2.052\" data-title=\"KEY SYNC on the deck\"><ol class=\"mn-steps\"><li data-t=\"500\">Hold <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> on the left deck and press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"sync\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/sync.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"75.39\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SYNC<\/span><\/span> on the left deck<\/li><\/ol><\/li><li data-flow=\"physical-double-shift-1\" data-video=\"assets/manual/nav/physical-double-shift-1.mp4\" data-poster=\"assets/manual/nav/physical-double-shift-1.webp\" data-w=\"1280\" data-h=\"480\" data-seconds=\"2.912\" data-title=\"Left side\"><ol class=\"mn-steps\"><li data-t=\"500\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> on the left deck twice quickly<\/li><\/ol><\/li><\/ol><\/div>\n<figure class=\"mf mf--hw\" id=\"f-hardware-3\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">XDJ-XZ deck<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/84f60f5edc5894c8.webp\" width=\"1000\" height=\"1211\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"One deck from above. The pads are named A to D on the top row and E to H on the bottom row.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"15.900\" data-y=\"53.757\" aria-label=\"1: SHIFT\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-3-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"85.000\" data-y=\"34.021\" aria-label=\"2: SYNC\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-3-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"86.900\" data-y=\"55.904\" aria-label=\"3: MASTER TEMPO\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-3-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"90.600\" data-y=\"76.961\" aria-label=\"4: TEMPO slider\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-3-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"50.500\" data-y=\"40.380\" aria-label=\"5: Jog wheel\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-3-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"50.500\" data-y=\"73.741\" aria-label=\"6: Pad mode buttons\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-3-6\">6<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"7\" data-x=\"72.500\" data-y=\"73.741\" aria-label=\"7: BEAT JUMP\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-3-7\">7<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"8\" data-x=\"50.500\" data-y=\"81.585\" aria-label=\"8: Pads A to D\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-3-8\">8<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"9\" data-x=\"50.500\" data-y=\"90.091\" aria-label=\"9: Pads E to H\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-3-9\">9<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"10\" data-x=\"21.200\" data-y=\"83.898\" aria-label=\"10: CUE and PLAY/PAUSE\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-3-10\">10<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>One deck from above. The pads are named A to D on the top row and E to H on the bottom row.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-hardware-3-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>SHIFT<\/b> <span>Press twice quickly to switch this side between its two decks. Held, it is the modifier for the combinations below.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-hardware-3-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>SYNC<\/b> <span>SHIFT + SYNC matches this deck's key to the master deck (KEY SYNC). SYNC alone is stock on decks 1 and 2.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-hardware-3-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>MASTER TEMPO<\/b> <span>While KEY SYNC holds, a press returns the deck to its own key.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-hardware-3-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>TEMPO slider<\/b> <span>After you switch decks, the new deck keeps its tempo until the slider reaches it.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-hardware-3-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>Jog wheel<\/b> <span>Stock on decks 1 and 2. Plays decks 3 and 4, and the games.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-hardware-3-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>Pad mode buttons<\/b> <span>HOT CUE, BEAT LOOP, SLIP LOOP, BEAT JUMP. One of them gives stem pads. With SHIFT, they mute stems.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"7\" id=\"f-hardware-3-7\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">7<\/span><div><b>BEAT JUMP<\/b> <span>Press for beat jump page 1. SHIFT + BEAT JUMP gives page 2.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"8\" id=\"f-hardware-3-8\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">8<\/span><div><b>Pads A to D<\/b> <span>Stem pads in the stem mode when the bank is A-D. Jump pairs A/B and C/D in BEAT JUMP mode.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"9\" id=\"f-hardware-3-9\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">9<\/span><div><b>Pads E to H<\/b> <span>Stem pads when the bank is E-H. Jump pairs E/F and G/H in BEAT JUMP mode.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"10\" id=\"f-hardware-3-10\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">10<\/span><div><b>CUE and PLAY/PAUSE<\/b> <span>Stock on decks 1 and 2. They play deck 3 or 4 while the side drives it.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Key<\/th><th>Action with XZ Mods<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> twice<\/td><td>Switches the left side between deck 1 and deck 3, or the right side between deck 2 and deck 4. Press it twice within about half a second, without touching anything else. Decks 3 and 4 need the loopback cable; without it the screen says DECK 3 AND 4 NEED THE CH3/CH4 ROUTE.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> + <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"sync\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/sync.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"75.39\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SYNC<\/span><\/span><\/td><td>KEY SYNC: shifts the key of the deck this side controls to match the master deck, and turns on MASTER TEMPO. Press it again to end KEY SYNC. Works on all four decks. <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"sync\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/sync.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"75.39\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SYNC<\/span><\/span> alone keeps its stock job on decks 1 and 2.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"master-tempo\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/master-tempo.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"142.24\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MASTER TEMPO<\/span><\/span><\/td><td>While KEY SYNC holds on that deck, a press ends KEY SYNC and returns the deck to its own key. Otherwise stock. <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> + <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"master-tempo\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/master-tempo.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"142.24\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MASTER TEMPO<\/span><\/span> keeps its stock job.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"hot-cue\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/hot-cue.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"78.51\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">HOT CUE<\/span><\/span>, <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"beat-loop\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/beat-loop.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"94.73\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BEAT LOOP<\/span><\/span>, <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"slip-loop\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/slip-loop.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"89.54\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SLIP LOOP<\/span><\/span><\/td><td>Choose the pad mode as on a stock player. The mode set in MODS &gt; STEMS &gt; STEM PADS turns four pads into stem pads.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> + <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"hot-cue\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/hot-cue.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"78.51\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">HOT CUE<\/span><\/span><\/td><td>Mutes or unmutes the first stem in your STEM ORDER (vocals by default) on that deck.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> + <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"beat-loop\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/beat-loop.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"94.73\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BEAT LOOP<\/span><\/span><\/td><td>Mutes or unmutes the second stem (harmonics by default).<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> + <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"slip-loop\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/slip-loop.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"89.54\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SLIP LOOP<\/span><\/span><\/td><td>Mutes or unmutes the third stem (drums by default).<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"beat-jump\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/beat-jump.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96.53\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BEAT JUMP<\/span><\/span><\/td><td>Beat jump mode with page 1 of your jump sizes.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> + <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"beat-jump\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/beat-jump.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96.53\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BEAT JUMP<\/span><\/span><\/td><td>Beat jump mode with page 2 of your jump sizes. Let go of <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> before you press a pad.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>TEMPO slider<\/td><td>After a deck switch, the deck that takes over keeps its tempo until the slider crosses its value. Then the slider moves it again. This works both ways.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"load\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/load.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"100.66\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">LOAD<\/span><\/span><\/td><td>Loads into the deck the side controls now.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Jog wheel<\/td><td>Stock on decks 1 and 2. On decks 3 and 4 it bends, scratches in VINYL mode and moves loop edges. The jog games use it too.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>The three SHIFT + pad mode combinations work while the USB loader has the stem engine. They also turn stem audio on if it was off. With them, the stock SHIFT + HOT CUE (CALL) is not available on decks 1 and 2.<\/p>\n<p>Every other deck key keeps its stock job on decks 1 and 2. While a side drives deck 3 or 4, the transport, loop, cue and tempo keys play that software deck instead. <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"four-decks\">Four decks<\/a> lists what each one does there.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-performance-pads\" data-anchor=\"performance-pads\">Performance pads<\/h3>\n<p>The eight pads keep their stock job in every pad mode, with two exceptions: the stem pads, and the BEAT JUMP pads.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mn\" data-iface=\"modern\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Performance pads\"><ol class=\"mn-scenes\"><li data-flow=\"physical-pad-mode-pages\" data-video=\"assets/manual/nav/physical-pad-mode-pages.mp4\" data-poster=\"assets/manual/nav/physical-pad-mode-pages.webp\" data-w=\"1280\" data-h=\"480\" data-seconds=\"3.852\" data-title=\"Performance pads\"><ol class=\"mn-steps\"><li data-t=\"500\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"hot-cue\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/hot-cue.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"78.51\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">HOT CUE<\/span><\/span> on the left deck<\/li><li data-t=\"800\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"beat-loop\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/beat-loop.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"94.73\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BEAT LOOP<\/span><\/span> on the left deck<\/li><li data-t=\"1100\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"slip-loop\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/slip-loop.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"89.54\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SLIP LOOP<\/span><\/span> on the left deck<\/li><li data-t=\"1400\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"beat-jump\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/beat-jump.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96.53\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BEAT JUMP<\/span><\/span> on the left deck<\/li><li data-t=\"1700\">Hold <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> on the left deck and press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"hot-cue\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/hot-cue.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"78.51\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">HOT CUE<\/span><\/span> on the left deck, then <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"beat-loop\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/beat-loop.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"94.73\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BEAT LOOP<\/span><\/span> on the left deck, then <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"slip-loop\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/slip-loop.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"89.54\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SLIP LOOP<\/span><\/span> on the left deck<\/li><\/ol><\/li><\/ol><\/div>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Pad mode<\/th><th>Pads with XZ Mods<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>HOT CUE<\/td><td>Stock hot cues. Gate cue and smart cue change what a hot cue does when you turn them on; see <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"performance\" data-anchor=\"gate-cue-and-smart-cue\">Gate cue and smart cue<\/a>.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>BEAT LOOP<\/td><td>Stock beat loops.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>SLIP LOOP<\/td><td>Stock slip loops.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>BEAT JUMP<\/td><td>Your jump sizes. A/B, C/D, E/F and G/H are pairs: the first pad jumps back, the second forward. With a loop on, the loop moves instead. <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> + pad keeps its stock job on decks 1 and 2. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"performance\" data-anchor=\"beat-jump\">Beat jump<\/a>.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The stem mode<\/td><td>Four pads (A to D, or E to H) mute stems instead. The other four keep their job in that mode.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<h4 id=\"m-stem-pads\" data-anchor=\"stem-pads\">Stem pads<\/h4>\n<p>In the pad mode you choose for stems, four pads switch stems on that deck. A, B and C mute the three stems in your STEM ORDER. D is BYPASS: it plays the original track instead of the stems. On a 4-stem track, D mutes bass instead. With the E-H bank, E to H do the same.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mn\" data-iface=\"modern\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Stem pads\"><ol class=\"mn-scenes\"><li data-flow=\"stem-pads-values\" data-video=\"assets/manual/nav/stem-pads-values.mp4\" data-poster=\"assets/manual/nav/stem-pads-values.webp\" data-w=\"1280\" data-h=\"480\" data-seconds=\"7.732\" data-title=\"In MODS\"><ol class=\"mn-steps\"><li data-t=\"500\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span><\/li><li data-t=\"1000\">Tap <strong>STEMS<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"1520\">Tap <strong>STEM PADS<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"2040\">Tap <strong>HOT CUE<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"2560\">Tap <strong>BEAT LOOP<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"3080\">Tap <strong>SLIP LOOP<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"3600\">Tap <strong>BEAT JUMP<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"4120\">Tap <strong>PADS A-D<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"4640\">Tap <strong>PADS E-H<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"5160\">Tap <strong>ORDER<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"5680\">Tap <strong>STEM COLOURS<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"6200\">Tap <strong>OFF<\/strong><\/li><\/ol><\/li><li data-flow=\"physical-stem-pads\" data-video=\"assets/manual/nav/physical-stem-pads.mp4\" data-poster=\"assets/manual/nav/physical-stem-pads.webp\" data-w=\"1280\" data-h=\"480\" data-seconds=\"3.312\" data-title=\"On the pads\"><ol class=\"mn-steps\"><li data-t=\"500\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"hot-cue\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/hot-cue.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"78.51\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">HOT CUE<\/span><\/span> on the left deck<\/li><li data-t=\"800\">Press pad A on the left deck<\/li><li data-t=\"1100\">Press pad B on the left deck<\/li><li data-t=\"1400\">Press pad C on the left deck<\/li><li data-t=\"1700\">Press pad D on the left deck<\/li><li data-t=\"2000\">Press pad A on the left deck<\/li><\/ol><\/li><\/ol><\/div>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-hardware-4\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODS · STEM PADS<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/d734197fbb0802b2.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"HOT CUE gives stem pads on A to D, in the default order, with stem colours on the pad lights.\" data-iface=\"modern\"><img src=\"manual/shots/d6eefdf3a54c8f84.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"HOT CUE gives stem pads on A to D, in the default order, with stem colours on the pad lights.\" data-iface=\"classic\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"51.250\" data-y=\"11.458\" aria-label=\"1: Pad mode\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-4-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"46.250\" data-y=\"30.208\" aria-label=\"2: Pad diagram\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-4-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"71.500\" data-y=\"29.792\" aria-label=\"3: STEMS ON\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-4-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"88.250\" data-y=\"42.917\" aria-label=\"4: Order\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-4-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"89.000\" data-y=\"59.583\" aria-label=\"5: Stem pad lights\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-4-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"89.750\" data-y=\"88.542\" aria-label=\"6: Works on\" aria-describedby=\"f-hardware-4-6\">6<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>HOT CUE gives stem pads on A to D, in the default order, with stem colours on the pad lights.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-hardware-4-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>Pad mode<\/b> <span>The pad mode button that gives stem pads. The others keep their pads.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-hardware-4-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>Pad diagram<\/b> <span>What each pad does in that mode, laid out like the pads on the deck.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-hardware-4-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>STEMS ON<\/b> <span>Which four pads carry the stems: PADS A-D or PADS E-H.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-hardware-4-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>Order<\/b> <span>The order of the stems on pads A, B and C and on the play screen. Push, then turn to change it.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-hardware-4-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>Stem pad lights<\/b> <span>STEM COLOURS lights stem pads in their stem colours and dims muted stems. OFF leaves the pad lights to the player.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-hardware-4-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>Works on<\/b> <span>Stem pads work on decks 1 and 2. Decks 3 and 4 have no stems.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Setting on this page<\/th><th>Choices<\/th><th>Default<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>Pad mode<\/td><td>HOT CUE, BEAT LOOP, SLIP LOOP, BEAT JUMP<\/td><td>HOT CUE<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>STEMS ON<\/td><td>PADS A-D, PADS E-H<\/td><td>PADS A-D<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>STEM PAD LIGHTS<\/td><td>STEM COLOURS, OFF<\/td><td>STEM COLOURS<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>If you choose BEAT JUMP for stems, beat jumps win its pads. Page 2 always jumps. Page 1 jumps while it uses MY SIZES, and gives stem pads only while page 1 is set to STOCK. <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"stems\">Stems<\/a> explains the stem audio itself, the order and the stem buttons on the screen.<\/p>\n<h4 id=\"m-pad-lights\" data-anchor=\"pad-lights\">Pad lights<\/h4>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>What you see<\/th><th>Meaning<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>Stem pads in stem colours, muted stems dim<\/td><td>STEM PAD LIGHTS is STEM COLOURS, on decks 1 and 2.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Warm red and amber pads in BEAT JUMP mode<\/td><td>Beat jump page 2 is selected on that deck.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Stock pad colours<\/td><td>Every other mode, and page 1 of BEAT JUMP.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<h3 id=\"m-decks-3-and-4-from-the-deck-controls\" data-anchor=\"decks-3-and-4-from-the-deck-controls\">Decks 3 and 4 from the deck controls<\/h3>\n<p>Each side of the XZ drives one of two decks: the left side deck 1 or deck 3, the right side deck 2 or deck 4. Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> twice to switch. <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"load\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/load.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"100.66\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">LOAD<\/span><\/span> on that side then loads into the deck it controls.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mn\" data-iface=\"modern\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Decks 3 and 4 from the deck controls\"><ol class=\"mn-scenes\"><li data-flow=\"physical-double-shift-2\" data-video=\"assets/manual/nav/physical-double-shift-2.mp4\" data-poster=\"assets/manual/nav/physical-double-shift-2.webp\" data-w=\"1280\" data-h=\"480\" data-seconds=\"2.912\" data-title=\"Decks 3 and 4 from the deck controls\"><ol class=\"mn-steps\"><li data-t=\"500\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> on the right deck twice quickly<\/li><\/ol><\/li><\/ol><\/div>\n<ol class=\"steps\"><li>Connect the loopback cable and wait until MODS &gt; 4 DECKS says the route is ready.<\/li><li>Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> twice quickly on the left side. The left side now drives deck 3.<\/li><li>Move the TEMPO slider until it reaches deck 3's tempo. Until then the slider does not change deck 3.<\/li><li>Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> twice again to go back to deck 1.<\/li><\/ol>\n<p>If the loopback route goes down, both sides go back to decks 1 and 2. <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"four-decks\">Four decks<\/a> covers setup, the deck view and every status.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-when-a-control-does-not-respond\" data-anchor=\"when-a-control-does-not-respond\">When a control does not respond<\/h3>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>What happens<\/th><th>Why, and what to do<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span> opens a stock menu instead of MODS<\/td><td>That screen has its own MENU job. Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"back\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/back.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"76.49\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BACK<\/span><\/span> to the play screen, then press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span>.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span> opens UTILITY<\/td><td>You held it. A short press opens MODS.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The button above <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"link\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/link.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"54.02\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">LINK<\/span><\/span> does nothing<\/td><td>It is set to NOTHING. Change it in MODS &gt; PLAY &gt; BUTTON ABOVE LINK.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shift\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shift.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHIFT<\/span><\/span> twice shows DECK 3 AND 4 NEED THE CH3/CH4 ROUTE<\/td><td>Decks 3 and 4 are not connected. Open MODS &gt; 4 DECKS.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The TEMPO slider does not change the deck<\/td><td>Pickup after a deck switch. Move the slider through the deck's tempo.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>A key sync press shows a message on the deck's key<\/td><td>See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"performance\" data-anchor=\"keys-and-key-sync\">Keys and KEY SYNC<\/a>.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>A BEAT JUMP pad shows JUMP UNAVAILABLE<\/td><td>See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"performance\" data-anchor=\"when-a-jump-is-refused\">When a jump is refused<\/a>.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>";
